  "initial_reflection": {
    "summary": "The run developed a useful exhaust, strength, and area-damage shell, but the deck became large and repetitive while the Collector fight was lost primarily through poor defensive prioritization at critical low-HP turns. The final fight reached turn 8 with only 26 HP and no block while both Torch Heads were attacking, despite several legal defensive options being available.",
    "lessons": [
      {
        "category": "COMBAT",
        "title": "Prioritize immediate survival over setup at low HP",
        "situation": "When HP is low, multiple enemies are attacking, and the player has little or no block, especially in a boss fight.",
        "lesson": "Take enough immediate block before spending energy on attacks, exhaust setup, or debuffs that do not prevent the current threat. In the final fight, use legal defensive cards such as Defend+ or Shrug It Off before continuing damage or setup.",
        "evidence_points": [
          "At turn 8, the player had 26/85 HP and 0 block while both Torch Heads had ATTACK intents; Defend+ was a legal alternative, but Disarm+ on the Collector was chosen first.",
          "After Disarm+, the player spent energy on Pommel Strike and only then played Defend+, ending the sequence at 8 block while still facing both attacking Torch Heads.",
